# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — Build Context Filter for Student Management API
#
# Docker sends the entire project directory to the Docker daemon as the "build
# context" during 'docker build' / 'docker compose build'. This file tells the
# daemon which paths to EXCLUDE from that context.
#
# Excluding unnecessary files:
#   - Reduces the build context size (faster COPY . . step)
#   - Prevents secrets (.env) from reaching the image
#   - Prevents dev artifacts (__pycache__, .venv, logs) from inflating image size
#   - Prevents cache-busting: excluding large files that never change in the
#     container stops Docker from invalidating the pip install cache layer
# =============================================================================

# ── Python artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bytecode and cache files are regenerated at runtime. Exclude them to keep
# the image clean and prevent stale .pyc files from entering the container.
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The container uses the system Python from the base image and installs
# dependencies via pip inside the image. A local .venv is irrelevant and would
# massively inflate the build context (hundreds of MB).
env/
venv/
.venv/
.python-version

# ── Build / distribution artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# ── Logs and databases ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logs are written at runtime and persisted via a bind mount (./logs:/app/logs).
# Including them in the image would bake stale log content into every build.
# SQLite databases are not used in production (Postgres is), so exclude them.
logs/
*.log
*.sqlite3
*.db

# ── Test and type-check caches ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ── Python history ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.python_history

# ── OS artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store

# ── Secrets — CRITICAL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env contains database passwords, JWT secrets, and other credentials.
# It must NEVER be baked into the image. Use 'env_file:' in compose.yaml or
# runtime environment injection instead.
.env

# ── Version control ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .git contains the full commit history — hundreds of MB that have no place
# in a runtime container. Also prevents accidental secret exposure via git log.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ── Docker files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Dockerfile itself and compose.yaml are build-time/orchestration files.
# They don't belong inside the running container image.
Dockerfile
dockerfile
compose.yaml
compose.yml
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.yaml

# ── Supporting / dev-only files ───────────────────────────────────────────────
Supporting Files/

# ── Editor and IDE configuration ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
